      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nThe order may contain a typo. The usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg once daily, and the usual maintenance range is 50\u2013200 mg once daily.\n\nAlso, orders like this normally come from a licensed prescriber. If a clinician on the medicine service wants this drug, they should confirm the intended dose and enter or co-sign the order.\n\nIf you give me a corrected dose, for example 50 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it. If a prescriber really does intend 1000 mg, they should verify it with pharmacy first."
